ssues we saw in Aurora v2. On top of that, it costs us 1/6 of what we were paying with AWS.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="mt-5 flex h-[30px] items-center justify-center lg:mt-[18px] md:h-auto md:flex-col md:gap-2.5"><img alt="Cody Jenkins photo" width="30" height="30" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="mr-2.5 rounded-full md:mx-auto" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fcody-jenkins.12-u~sf5u8n1d.jpg&amp;w=32&amp;q=100&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fcody-jenkins.12-u~sf5u8n1d.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=100&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Fcody-jenkins.12-u~sf5u8n1d.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=100&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/><span class="text-lg leading-tight font-light tracking-extra-tight text-gray-new-70 lg:text-base md:mx-auto md:flex md:flex-col md:items-center md:gap-1 md:text-center md:text-sm"><span>Cody Jenkins</span><cite class="ml-1.5 text-gray-new-50 not-italic before:mr-1.5 before:inline-flex before:h-px before:w-4 before:bg-gray-new-50 before:align-middle md:ml-0 md:before:hidden">Head of Engineering at Invenco</cite></span></figcaption></figure></div></div><section class="features mt-[200px] safe-paddings xl:mt-40 lg:mt-32 md:mt-24"><div class="relative mx-auto lg:max-w-none lg:px-8 md:px-5 max-w-6xl px-8 xl:px-8! md:px-5!"><div class="flex gap-10 rounded-2xl lg:flex-wrap lg:gap-12 md:gap-10"><h2 class="min-w-[360px] font-title text-[44px] leading-none font-medium tracking-extra-tight xl:min-w-[312px] xl:text-4xl lg:max-w-[440px] lg:text-[32px] md:text-[28px]">Hundreds of Enterprises are switching to Neon. Here’s why</h2><ul class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-[26px] gap-y-11 xl:gap-x-[30px] lg:gap-10 md:grid-cols-1 md:gap-8"><li class="flex flex-col"><div class="flex items-center gap-x-2"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="22" height="22" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="shrink-0" style=